course: dictionary
lesson: 15082
title: Ripening: becoming ready
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ripening means becoming ripe. A ripe fruit is ready to eat: it is soft, sweet and has its proper colour. «The pears are ripening on the tree, so we will pick them on Sunday.» The words «on the tree» and «pick them» give you a clue that the pears are not ready yet, but are getting closer to being ready.
explain: Ripening is a process, so it happens over time, not all at once. «The tomatoes are ripening in the sun, and each day they turn a little redder.» The word «each day» tells you the change is slow and gradual.
explain: You can also use ripening for something that is slowly getting ready, like an idea. «My plan has been ripening for weeks, and now I am ready to share it.» Here the plan is not a fruit, but it is still developing over time, just as a fruit does.
fact: Ripening means becoming ready to eat, soft, sweet and coloured.
fact: Ripening is the -ing form of the verb ripen: ripen, ripens, ripened, ripening.
fact: Bananas change from green to yellow as they ripen.
fact: Ripening fruit gives off a gas called ethylene.
fact: Putting an unripe avocado in a bag with a banana can speed up its ripening, because the banana gives off ethylene.
exercise: «The apples are ripening on the tree.» What does ripening mean here? | Shrinking in the cold | Turning into juice | *Becoming ready to eat | Falling to the ground
exercise: «The corn is ripening in the sun.» Which season is the corn ripening in? | *Late summer | Winter | The middle of the night | Early spring
exercise: «The bananas turned from green to yellow as they ripened.» What colour change shows the bananas are ripening? | *Green to yellow | Green to blue | Yellow to black | Red to white
test: Ripening fruit gives off which gas? | *Ethylene | Steam | Oxygen | Salt
test: Putting an unripe avocado in a bag with a banana does what? | Makes it freeze | Turns it blue | *Speeds up the ripening | Stops the ripening
exam: «My plan has been ripening for months, and now it is nearly ready.» What does ripening mean in this sentence? | Falling apart | *Slowly getting ready | Going mouldy | Shrinking away
